<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tuluva dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1505–c. 1570</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tuluva dynasty was the third ruling house of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijayanagara-empire">Vijayanagara Empire</a>, founded when Vira Narasimha, son of the general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narasa-nayaka">Narasa Nayaka</a>, took the throne in 1505. Under his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishnadevaraya">Krishnadevaraya</a> (r. 1509–1529) the empire reached its height. Later Tuluva kings were dominated by the regent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aliya-rama-raya">Aliya Rama Raya</a>, and after the defeat at Talikota in 1565 the Aravidu family took over.</p></div>
